  "notes": "`token_count` is what §6.2's ceiling is applied to, and this is the message the clause's own example describes — \"two submessages per end-point\", four in all. Here it equals the length of `tokens`, because the first submessage is text; `readings/36` is where the two differ, which is the reason the count is an expectation of its own rather than something a runner derives from the list."
